{"visualAudit":"01-candidates","data":{"grades":[{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":4,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":4,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption should name the fishpond in the foreground and the ruined church beyond, and note the 1993 date."],"reason":"Strongest choice: it shows both features named in the Examples text, the former fishpond and the ruined church, in their empty valley setting. That conveys desertion better than the church-only views.","id":"6585802","total":18,"accepted":true},{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":3,"composition":4,"thumbnailClarity":4,"contextualFit":3,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption should mention the missing aisles and roofless tower, so readers don't mistake the church for an intact building."],"reason":"A clear, well-lit view of St Martin's Church. Part of the nave still has a roof, so the ruin reads less obviously than in the interior view, and the deserted village setting is absent.","id":"13199240","total":18,"accepted":true},{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":3,"composition":4,"thumbnailClarity":4,"contextualFit":3,"problems":[],"improvements":["Use only as a second image beside the fishpond view, with a caption naming the roofless interior."],"reason":"The open sky through the roofless interior shows the ruin unmistakably. It covers only the church, not the fishpond or village site, and partly duplicates the other church view.","id":"183989393","total":18,"accepted":true}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5-5","images":[{"id":"6585802","title":"Wharram Percy Geograph.jpg","description":"Picture of Wharram Percey, from this image at Geograph.org.uk.\nSubmitted to that site by Paul Allison\nTaken in 1993\n\nDescription: Deserted Medieval Village, Looking north from old Fish Pond","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Wharram_Percy_Geograph.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wharram_Percy_Geograph.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wharram_Percy_Geograph.jpg/500px-Wharram_Percy_Geograph.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"The original uploader was Nyh at English Wikipedia.","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"},{"id":"13199240","title":"Wharram Percy, St Martins Church - geograph.org.uk - 659805.jpg","description":"Ruin of St Martin's parish church, Wharram Percy, Ryedale, Yorkshire: view from the southeast, showing the chancel","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Wharram_Percy%2C_St_Martins_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_659805.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wharram_Percy,_St_Martins_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_659805.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Wharram_Percy%2C_St_Martins_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_659805.jpg/500px-Wharram_Percy%2C_St_Martins_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_659805.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"dennis smith","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"},{"id":"183989393","title":"Wharram Percy Church.jpg","description":"The church interior, looking towards the tower","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f5/Wharram_Percy_Church.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wharram_Percy_Church.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Wharram_Percy_Church.jpg/500px-Wharram_Percy_Church.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"HallCastleKing","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}]}}
