{"visualAudit":"03-candidates","data":{"grades":[{"subjectMatch":0,"learningValue":1,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":0,"problems":["Shows a 1900 ploughing match in Sydney, Australia, not English medieval ridge and furrow or desertion."],"reason":"A clear photograph, but of the wrong place, period and farming practice. It would mislead readers about medieval fields.","id":"5123700","total":7,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":3,"learningValue":3,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":3,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption it as ridge and furrow at Cold Newton, Leicestershire, a deserted village site, if the metadata confirms this."],"reason":"Ground-level ridges are clearly visible in raking light and illustrate the surviving pattern the paragraph mentions, but it shows fields only, not the village.","id":"12654906","total":15,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":2,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":2,"problems":["Scottish rig near Airdrie with no link to a deserted village or medieval date; its ties to the English enclosure narrative are unproven."],"reason":"Curving rigs show well, but the site is a generic Scottish example of uncertain date.","id":"69925256","total":12,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":4,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":4,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption it to point out the house platforms and the surrounding ridge and furrow, and crop the blue corner bands."],"reason":"Strongest choice: the lidar of the deserted Wormleighton village shows house plots beside ridge and furrow, linking desertion to the field pattern. The photographs show fields only.","id":"175307008","total":18,"accepted":true},{"subjectMatch":1,"learningValue":2,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":1,"problems":["The title names a Roman fort, not a deserted medieval village; the fort is barely discernible among the ridges."],"reason":"Ridge and furrow is clear, but the subject is a Roman fort, which confuses the section.","id":"177557380","total":10,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":2,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":2,"problems":["Northumberland hill landscape with no stated deserted village; the cultivation terraces are not tied to desertion."],"reason":"Detailed lidar of ridges on a hillside, but it lacks any village link, unlike the Wormleighton lidar.","id":"178530545","total":12,"accepted":false}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5-5","images":[{"id":"5123700","title":"Ploughing match from The Powerhouse Museum Collection.jpg","description":"\"Ploughing Match\", Sydney, Australia, around 1900 – Silver gelatin dry plate glass negative in landscape format. The image depicts a ploughing competition at what appears to be an agricultural show. The competition is between teams of two-horse single-furrow mouldboard ploughs. Five teams are depicted in the image and numerous strips of alterate furrowed and unfurrowed land can be seen. One of the plough teams is depicted in the foregound of the image. The team consists of two horses harnessed to a single-furrow mouldboard plough which is hand controlled by a man walking behind the plough. A man can be seen in the foreground on the left side of the image, he is holding an axe and looking towards the plough team. Crowds of people can be seen in the background of the image. The crowds appear to be attending an agricultural show. Horse drawn vehicles and horses can also be seen in the background. A hill is depicted in the far background of the image. The caption, studio number and studio mark are inscribed on the reverse of the negative. 55/61 Tyrrell Inventory Number, 132 Kerry Studio Number.","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Ploughing_match_from_The_Powerhouse_Museum_Collection.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ploughing_match_from_The_Powerhouse_Museum_Collection.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ploughing_match_from_The_Powerhouse_Museum_Collection.jpg/500px-Ploughing_match_from_The_Powerhouse_Museum_Collection.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Charles Kerry","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":""},{"id":"12654906","title":"Cold Newton ridge and furrow.jpg","description":"Cold Newton ridge and furrow","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Cold_Newton_ridge_and_furrow.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cold_Newton_ridge_and_furrow.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Cold_Newton_ridge_and_furrow.jpg/500px-Cold_Newton_ridge_and_furrow.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Matt Neale from UK","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"},{"id":"69925256","title":"Blackhillrig1.jpg","description":"An example of rig and furrow. This image is from the area around rough rig reservoir near Airdrie Scotland. Here you will find some of the best examples in the UK.","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Blackhillrig1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blackhillrig1.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Blackhillrig1.jpg/500px-Blackhillrig1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Kevthedev","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"},{"id":"175307008","title":"Deserted Medieval Village, Wormleighton in Warwickshire.jpg","description":"A lidar image derived from Environmental Agency open source data.gov.uk data (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/) via the houseprices.io lidar map.","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Deserted_Medieval_Village%2C_Wormleighton_in_Warwickshire.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deserted_Medieval_Village,_Wormleighton_in_Warwickshire.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Deserted_Medieval_Village%2C_Wormleighton_in_Warwickshire.jpg/500px-Deserted_Medieval_Village%2C_Wormleighton_in_Warwickshire.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Dr John Wells","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"},{"id":"177557380","title":"Hunnum Roman fort and immediate landscape.jpg","description":"A lidar image derived from Environmental Agency open source data.gov.uk data (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/) via the houseprices.io lidar map.","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Hunnum_Roman_fort_and_immediate_landscape.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hunnum_Roman_fort_and_immediate_landscape.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Hunnum_Roman_fort_and_immediate_landscape.jpg/500px-Hunnum_Roman_fort_and_immediate_landscape.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Dr John Wells","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"},{"id":"178530545","title":"Heddon Hill west of Brandon in Northumberland.jpg","description":"A lidar image derived from Environmental Agency open source data.gov.uk data (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/